## Control {{controlId}}: Enforce Safeguarding Measures for CUI at Alternate Work Sites

**Implementation Status:** {{status}}

This organization enforces CUI safeguarding at alternate work sites for the {{tenantName}} M365 GCC High tenant through telework security policies, Conditional Access enforcement, and device compliance requirements documented in "Alternate Work Site Policy v1.0" maintained by {{variables.systemAdministrator}}.

{{#if conditionalAccessActive}}
**Technical Safeguards:**
{{caPoliciesTotalCount}} Conditional Access policies enforce security requirements for remote CUI access:
{{#each policies}}
- **{{displayName}}** ({{state}}): Requires {{#each grantControls.builtInControls}}{{this}}{{#unless @last}}, {{/unless}}{{/each}}
{{/each}}

Remote access requires compliant device, MFA authentication, and approved network location before CUI access is granted.
{{/if}}

**Alternate Work Site Requirements:**
- CUI materials (digital and paper) stored in locked containers when not in active use
- CUI displayed on screens in private areas only; screen privacy filters required in shared spaces
- CUI conversations conducted in private areas; speakerphone use prohibited in shared spaces
- Printing of CUI at alternate sites prohibited unless secure printing infrastructure is available
- VPN required for all CUI system access from alternate locations

**Personnel Responsibilities:**
- Telework agreement signed by all personnel accessing CUI from alternate sites
- Annual acknowledgment of alternate work site safeguarding requirements
- Incident reporting for any CUI spillage or unauthorized exposure at alternate locations

**Operational Procedure:**
- **Action:** Annual review of telework agreements; spot-check compliance during security assessments
- **Frequency:** Annual agreement renewal, continuous technical enforcement
- **Responsible Party:** {{variables.systemAdministrator}}
- **Documentation:** Alternate Work Site Policy v1.0, Telework Agreement Form PE-006

**Review Frequency:** Annually by ISSO

**Verification Method:** Examine telework agreements, Conditional Access policy configurations, device compliance reports, and alternate site security acknowledgments.

